# Workflow

Apply this rule manually when committing or opening a pull request.

## Commits
- Git commit messages are English. Example: `feat: add username login support`.
- Focus the message on why the change exists.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, PEMs, production keys).
- No `console.log` in production code. No TypeScript `any` (use `unknown`).
- Sensitive operations need audit events where the domain already requires them.

## Pull requests
Land changes through a pull request. Do not push directly to `main` or `master`. A push to those branches starts staging deploy (`docs/CI_CD.md`).

- Focused PRs; clear description of **why**.
- Unit tests pass. Integration tests pass when applicable.
- No hardcoded user-facing strings (use i18n). POS UI stays German (de-DE); Admin UI uses `frontend-admin/src/i18n/`.
- For medium or large changes, include a short implementation plan, affected files, main risks, backward compatibility impact, and a test strategy.
- After OpenAPI changes: `node scripts/generate-backend-openapi.mjs`, then `cd frontend-admin && npm run generate:api`, then `node scripts/verify-api-client.mjs`.

## Development Workflow

### Local Setup
1. Start PostgreSQL (Docker or local)
2. `npm install` at repo root (workspaces + Husky prepare)
3. Configure backend user-secrets (see `backend/README.md`)
4. `npm run dev` (API+Admin) — or `dev:all` / `dev:backend` / `dev:admin` / `dev:pos` / `dev:sites`

## Quick Reference

### Useful Commands
```bash
# From repo root (npm workspaces)
npm install
npm run dev                 # parallel RAM-safe: backend + admin (+ orphan cleanup)
npm run dev:all             # parallel full: backend + admin + POS + sites
npm run dev:cleanup         # kill leftover Next/Expo node workers
npm run dev:cleanup:orphans # kill only `.next/dev/build` workers (safe while apps run)
npm run dev:backend | dev:admin | dev:pos | dev:sites
npm run test
npm run verify:api-client
npm run generate:api
npm run install:git-hooks   # Husky → verify-api-client on commit

# Backend
dotnet run --project backend/KasseAPI_Final.csproj
dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project backend
dotnet test backend/KasseAPI_Final.sln

# Frontend Admin / POS / Sites
cd frontend-admin && npm run dev
cd frontend-admin && npm run generate:api
cd frontend && npm run dev
cd frontend-sites && npm run dev   # :3001
```

